":"June 14, 2026"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-clock w-3.5 h-3.5","children":[["$","circle","1mglay",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"}],["$","polyline","68esgv",{"points":"12 6 12 12 16 14"}],"$undefined"]}]," ",6," min read"]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"relative h-72 md:h-96 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden mb-10 shadow-md","children":["$","$L3",null,{"src":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1455619452474-d2be8b1e70cd?w=800&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80","alt":"Spice Secrets: Inside Our Thai Green Curry","fill":true,"className":"object-cover"}]}],["$","blockquote",null,{"className":"border-l-4 border-[#8B0000] pl-5 mb-8 bg-[#FFF8F0] py-4 pr-4 rounded-r-xl","children":["$","p",null,{"className":"text-base text-[#4a3820] italic leading-relaxed","children":"The Spicy Thai Green Curry is our most-loved vegetarian dish. Here's what goes into making it authentically bold and aromatic."}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col gap-4 mb-10","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-sm text-[#4a3820] leading-7","children":["Thai green curry is one of the most complex dishes in our menu — a harmony of heat, creaminess, and fragrant aromatics that must be carefully balanced."]}],["$","h3","1",{"className":"text-lg font-extrabold text-[#8B0000] mt-6 mb-2","children":"The Paste"}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-sm text-[#4a3820] leading-7","children":["We make our green curry paste from scratch. Fresh green chillies, lemongrass, galangal, kaffir lime zest, coriander root, white pepper, and shrimp paste (we offer a vegan version with miso) are pounded together in a stone mortar until completely smooth. This takes about 15 minutes — a food processor simply doesn't release the essential oils the same way."]}],["$","h3","3",{"className":"text-lg font-extrabold text-[#8B0000] mt-6 mb-2","children":"The Coconut Milk"}],["$","p","4",{"className":"text-sm text-[#4a3820] leading-7","children":["We use full-fat coconut milk from Thailand. The paste is fried in the thick cream that rises to the top of the can before the rest of the coconut milk is added. This \"cracking\" step intensifies the flavour dramatically."]}],["$","h3","5",{"className":"text-lg font-extrabold text-[#8B0000] mt-6 mb-2","children":"The Vegetables"}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-sm text-[#4a3820] leading-7","children":["Bamboo shoots, Thai aubergine, baby courgette, and fresh spinach are added in stages according to their cooking times. Nothing is overcooked — every vegetable retains its colour and texture."]}],["$","h3","7",{"className":"text-lg font-extrabold text-[#8B0000] mt-6 mb-2","children":"The Finish"}],["$","p","8",{"className":"text-sm text-[#4a3820] leading-7","children":["Fish sauce (or soy sauce for the vegan version), palm sugar, and fresh Thai basil leaves are stirred in at the last moment. The result is a curry that is simultaneously hot, sweet, salty, and fragrant."]}],["$","p","9",{"className":"text-sm text-[#4a3820] leading-7","children":["Order it with jasmine rice — the gentle floral fragrance of the rice is the perfect complement."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-12 pt-6 border-t border-[#C8A055]/20","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1 text-xs text-[#a09070]","children":[["$","svg",null,{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":24,"height":24,"viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":2,"strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-tag w-3.5 h-3.5","children":[["$","path","vktsd0",{"d":"M12.586 2.586A2 2 0 0 0 11.172 2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v7.172a2 2 0 0 0 .586 1.414l8.704 8.704a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 3.42 0l6.58-6.58a2.426 2.426 0 0 0 0-3.42z"}],["$","circle","kqv944